# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# Environment — never commit real secrets (SRS §27)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# Runtime storage (SRS §26)
#
# `**/` is load-bearing, and its absence was a real defect. A pattern with a slash anywhere but at the
# end is **anchored to this file's directory**, so `storage/logs/` matched only `<repo>/storage/logs/`
# — a path that does not exist — and never `backend/storage/logs/`, which is the one that does. Eleven
# runtime files were tracked as a result: ten rotated log archives and one uploaded student photo. The
# logs are not inert either: `MAIL_DRIVER=log` renders every outgoing message into them, and
# `mailService.js` says so in its own header — *"a reset link appears in `storage/logs`"*.
#
# Found in session 28 by noticing a `git commit` summary that named three `.log.gz` files.
**/storage/logs/
**/storage/uploads/
**/storage/backups/
**/storage/tmp/
*.log
*.log.gz
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Build output
backend/dist/
frontend/.next/
frontend/out/
frontend/build/
.turbo/

# Test artefacts
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Editor / OS
.vscode/*
